  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 945 PM CST SAT NOV 14 2026\n\nAn expansive surface high-pressure system centered over the\neastern U.S. will remain in control. Tonight, light winds and\nclear skies associated with the weakening surface pressure\ngradient along the ridge axis will promote strong radiational\ncooling. Consequently, a widespread frost and freeze is expected\nby Sunday morning, with low temperatures dropping into the upper\n20s to lower 30s area-wide. High cloud cover will gradually\nincrease on Sunday ahead of an approaching shortwave disturbance\nin the southern stream; however, dry low-level air and a\nsuppressed storm track should keep any measurable precipitation\nsouth of the forecast area through Monday morning.\n\nThis air mass will remain firmly in place over the coming days as\nhigh pressure settles over the Appalachians. Afternoon\ntemperatures will moderate gradually through Tuesday before\nwarmer conditions return Wednesday through Friday, with highs\nclimbing into the lower 70s as an upper-level ridge expands\nacross the region. Dry conditions are expected to persist through\nnext Saturday.\n\n16",
